text:
alice: Heads-up — SolarWind (dedicated pool) is hitting p99 tail spikes when KV-cache misses align with long sequences (~2k tokens). They're requesting a safe queue-signal + token budget proposal we can canary. Profiling attached to the thread.
ben: Can you paste a short perf sample? p50/p99 numbers and which kernel landed recently?
carlos: Profiling link: https://perf.redwood/sessions/9142 (private). Saw a regression after kernel 0.9.3 -> 0.9.4. Root cause looks like kernel selection changed for long-seq flows causing an extra memcpy on KV miss paths — increases per-token overhead and breaks batching grouping.
maya: Quick proposal (canary):
```json
{
  "queues": {
    "solarwind-high": {
      "max_queue_tokens": 4000,
      "dispatch_min_tokens": 32,
      "token_budget_target": 3000,
      "queue_signal_thresholds": {
        "kv_miss_penalty": 0.6,
        "age_ms_warn": 20,
        "age_ms_hard": 60
      }
    },
    "solarwind-default": {
      "max_queue_tokens": 2000,
      "dispatch_min_tokens": 16,
      "token_budget_target": 1200
    }
  },
  "continuous_batching": {
    "age_based_trimming_ms": 30,
    "group_by_prefix_cache": true
  },
  "fallback_kernel": "0.9.3"
}
```
maya: Plan: run a 10m canary pinned to fallback kernel 0.9.3, telemetry hooks + p99 alarm at 350ms. If green, ramp to 1h with metrics check.
ops-bot: Canary scheduled: 1992350000 — 10m window; telemetry hooks enabled; smoke tests passed.
ben: I'll apply the policy and enable age-based trimming param `max_age_ms=30`. If p99 > 350ms during canary, auto-revert and pin back to 0.9.3.
alice: Thanks — tagging SolarWind PM @jordan.solarwind so they're aware. Jordan: expect 10m canary then 1h ramp if green.
jordan.solarwind: Got it, we'll watch dashboards & share logs if anything odd.
maya: If canary shows any regression we'll revert and open kernel regression ticket for 0.9.4. Will also add a targeted profiler to capture KV miss memcpy hotspots.
ben: Ack :thumbsup:
ops-bot: Note: policy change will be applied to dedicated pool id `d-42-solarwind`. Canary job id `canary-1992350000-d42`.
